  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nukus 2 Wind and Battery Energy Storage Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project constitutes the development, construction, operation, and transfer of a 200-megawatt (MW) grid-connected wind power plant, a 100-megawatt-hour (MWh) battery energy storage system (BESS) and power evacuation infrastructure, comprised of a 220- kilovolt substation, an upgraded switchyard and Beruniy substation, and a 44-kilometer 110-kilovolt transmission line. It consists of 26 wind turbines, each with a capacity of 8 MW, a rotor diameter of 182 meters, and a hub height of 138 meters.</narrative>
  </description>
